      "anchor": {"section": "Plant Uses"},
      "note": "USGS records soaking Tilia americana inner bark in water to separate tough fibres, then using them for cordage and other fibre goods. This named-species modern regional account is analogical support for the bounded editorial linden-bast work relation; it establishes no Novgorod tree, bark, season, access, yield, or tool.",
      "review_status": "approved"
